        <mxCell id="note2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#666666;" value="None deferred queue is woken by an event. In ACID case, the dirty-clear event wakes waiting transactions directly. On the BASE side, both queues are polled instead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;The parent transactions in queue are retried again at every admission step. The repair queue is drained every repair batch, each ACID completion that releases locks,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;and each simulation step.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(102, 102, 102), rgb(149, 149, 149));&quot;&gt;The fixed step retry is needed because locks can also be released, for example when a group aborts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="44" width="1020" x="35" y="603" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bHfQResDobG4qqS1OE9H-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#a86a13;" value="if resource is&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;available, txn&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;added back to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;pending queue&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60.5" width="73" x="45" y="181.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
